From e83f2cd8c1fe2760a076bbcfc74aa7bff03aef79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 08:27:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Track X11 frame visibility for volume meters

GTK keeps a surface mapped when i3 hides its frame without publishing
_NET_WM_STATE_HIDDEN, so the generic mapped and suspended properties cannot
detect hidden workspaces.

Watch map, unmap, and reparent events for the window-manager frame through
GdkX11Display::xevent and use the client window viewability to control
peak-monitor streams.
